# Line endings.
#
# Store LF in the repository and check out LF on every platform, regardless of
# each developer's `core.autocrlf`. This machine has `core.autocrlf=true`, so
# without this file the working copy would be CRLF locally and LF in CI, which
# contradicts .editorconfig (`end_of_line = lf`) and makes diffs platform-
# dependent.
#
# This matters beyond tidiness: NFR-12 requires backtest results to reproduce
# byte-for-byte from a pinned dataset, and the golden TradingView CSV fixtures
# (TEST-1, TEST-13) are text files whose bytes must not depend on the machine
# that checked them out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files git should never try to normalise, in case content sniffing gets it
# wrong. Fixtures added in later phases are text (CSV) and are covered above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary

# Generated. Collapsed in review UIs, but deliberately still diffable locally:
# lockfile changes are a supply-chain surface (SEC-10) and should stay readable.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true
